Source offer for the bundled GCC runtime
========================================

The Nix release artifact links and, on train11, ships GCC 16.2.0's runtime
under the GNU GPL v3 with the GCC Runtime Library Exception 3.1:

  lib/libstdc++.so.6   shared, train11 layout
  lib/libgcc_s.so.1    shared, train11 layout
  wiz, grail           linked against these runtimes (lib/ on train11)

The GitHub release.yml path links Lean's static libc++ instead; see NOTICE
and LICENSES/lean4-third-party.

Corresponding Source
--------------------

The exact source is the nixpkgs gcc-16.2.0 derivation at the revision in
flake.lock, including nixpkgs' patches:

  nix build --no-link --print-out-paths \
    github:NixOS/nixpkgs/$(nix flake metadata --json |
      jq -r '.locks.nodes.nixpkgs.locked.rev')#gcc.src

Upstream tarball: https://ftp.gnu.org/gnu/gcc/gcc-16.2.0/gcc-16.2.0.tar.xz

The Wiz packaging scripts (scripts/release-tarball.sh,
scripts/scrub-store-paths.py) and the Wiz source are at
https://github.com/wiz-pl/wiz.

Written offer: for three years from the release date, the Wiz maintainers
will provide the Corresponding Source, including patches, on request at
https://github.com/wiz-pl/wiz/issues.

This file is the written offer for the runtime source. It ships as
share/wiz/SOURCE-OFFER next to the licence texts.
